        {
          "text": "Lists",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The list buttons in the Paragraph group start a bulleted or numbered list; items nest with Tab and Shift+Tab. Inside an item you can use bold, links, footnotes and inline math like any other text. Some things worth knowing:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Use a bulleted list for things with no order, such as an inventory or a set of options.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Use a numbered list for a procedure, where the order matters.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Nested lists change their bullet style on their own at each depth.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mathematics",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Equations group on the Insert tab holds it all. Inline math such as ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E = mc^2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is Ctrl+M; a displayed equation is Ctrl+Shift+M. The Equation builder (Ctrl+Shift+E) offers fractions, integrals, matrices and more as templates, and the Symbol palette (Ctrl+Shift+G) holds Greek letters, operators and arrows. A numbered, labelled equation:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} e^{-x^{2}}\\,dx = \\sqrt{\\pi}",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:gauss",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Multi-line derivations use the aligned environments. Here is the quadratic formula derived by completing the square:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\begin{align}\n  a x^2 + b x + c &= 0 \\\\\n  \\left(x + \\tfrac{b}{2a}\\right)^2 &= \\tfrac{b^2 - 4ac}{4a^2} \\\\\n  x &= \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n\\end{align}",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "To point back at an equation, use Cross-reference on the References tab and pick it from the list: Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:gauss",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the Gaussian integral above. If the equation is renumbered later, the reference follows.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
