      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thermal measurements",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The thermal conductivity was measured at 25 °C with a transient hot-wire probe embedded in each cylinder. A constant heating power ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "q",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " per unit length is applied to the wire and the temperature rise ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is recorded against time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". For an ideal line source in an infinite medium the conductivity follows from the slope of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " against ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\ln t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "k = \\frac{q}{4\\pi}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}\\,\\Delta T}{\\mathrm{d}\\ln t}\\right)^{-1}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:hotwire",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each value is the mean of five runs separated by 15 minutes to let the sample relax",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Only the window between 1 s and 10 s was fitted, to avoid wire-contact effects at early times and boundary effects at late times.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the uncertainty is the larger of the run-to-run scatter and the 3% calibration uncertainty of the probe.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Effective-medium model",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We compare the data with the Maxwell model for spherical inclusions of conductivity ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_f",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " at volume fraction ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\phi",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " in a matrix of conductivity ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "k_{\\mathrm{eff}} = k_m\\,\\frac{k_f + 2k_m + 2\\phi\\,(k_f - k_m)}{k_f + 2k_m - \\phi\\,(k_f - k_m)}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:maxwell",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "With ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " fixed at the measured value of the neat resin, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_f",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the only free parameter. It is found by minimising",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\chi^2(k_f) = \\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\left(\\frac{k_i - k_{\\mathrm{eff}}(\\phi_i; k_f)}{\\sigma_i}\\right)^2,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:chi2",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "over the ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N = 5",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " filled samples, where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_i",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\sigma_i",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " are the measured conductivity and its uncertainty.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "sec:results",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:results",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " lists the measured conductivities. The neat resin gives ",
