    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Frac.",
          "Meas.",
          "Model",
          "Gain"
        ],
        [
          "0.00",
          "0.20",
          "0.20",
          "1.00"
        ],
        [
          "0.05",
          "0.23",
          "0.23",
          "1.15"
        ],
        [
          "0.10",
          "0.27",
          "0.26",
          "1.35"
        ],
        [
          "0.15",
          "0.29",
          "0.30",
          "1.45"
        ],
        [
          "0.20",
          "0.34",
          "0.34",
          "1.70"
        ],
        [
          "0.30",
          "0.44",
          "0.44",
          "2.20"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Filler volume fraction (Frac.), measured and modelled thermal conductivity k (W/(m K)) at 25 °C, and enhancement over the neat resin. Uncertainties: 0.010 to 0.020 W/(m K). The model uses a filler conductivity of 9.7 W/(m K).",
      "label": "tab:results",
      "alignment": "rrrr",
      "style": "",
      "merges": [],
      "header": true,
      "repeat_header": false,
      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Minimising Eq. ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:chi2",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_f = 9.7\\ \\mathrm{W\\,m^{-1}\\,K^{-1}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\chi^2 = 1.4",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " for 4 degrees of freedom. The one-standard-deviation interval, 5.7 to 28 W/(m K), is asymmetric because the model saturates when ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "k_f \\gg k_m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". All model values in Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:results",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " lie within one standard deviation of the measurements.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "sec:discussion",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The fitted filler conductivity is much lower than the in-plane value of several hundred W/(m K) reported for single h-BN crystals ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "lindqvist2019"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". This is expected for randomly oriented platelets separated from the matrix by an interfacial thermal resistance, and it is consistent with other epoxy–ceramic composites ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "okafor2021",
            "tanaka2023"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Because Eq. ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:maxwell",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " is insensitive to ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
