      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each paper has one folder with three subfolders: ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "data",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " for raw files that are never edited, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "scripts",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " with one script per figure, and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "figures",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the output. A single build file lists which script produces which figure and rebuilds only what has changed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.2 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Version control",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scripts and the build file live in version control, and every commit message names the figure it changes. The raw data are too large for the repository, so we store their checksums instead and verify them before a build.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.3 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "A shared style",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "One style file sets font size, line widths and colours for all plots. Figure width is fixed to the column width of the target journal, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "w=8.6 \\mathrm{cm}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a single column, so that text in a figure appears at the same size as the body text.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "3 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "What it saved",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We timed the five steps of a typical figure update before and after the change, averaged over ten updates each (Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": ").",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Task",
          "Before (h)",
          "After (h)"
        ],
        [
          "Export data from the instrument",
          "0.5",
          "0.0"
        ],
        [
          "Re-plot with the new data",
          "1.5",
          "0.1"
        ],
        [
          "Restyle fonts and colours",
          "0.8",
          "0.1"
        ],
        [
          "Lay out the multi-panel figure",
          "0.5",
          "0.1"
        ],
        [
          "Check against the previous version",
          "0.2",
          "0.1"
        ],
        [
          "Total per update",
          "3.5",
          "0.4"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "",
      "label": null,
      "alignment": "",
      "style": "",
      "merges": [],
      "header": false,
      "repeat_header": false,
      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table 1: ",
          "marks": [
            "bold",
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Time for one figure update, in hours.",
          "marks": [
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "center",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The setup cost ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "C",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " was 24 h. If an update takes ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t_{\\mathrm{old}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " before and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t_{\\mathrm{new}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " after, the break-even number of updates is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N^{*}=\\frac{C}{t_{\\mathrm{old}}-t_{\\mathrm{new}}}=\\frac{24}{3.5-0.4}\\approx 7.7,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "so eight updates are enough, which one paper alone reaches. Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "(1)",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " ignores the benefit that matters most to us, namely that reviewers' requests for a changed axis no longer cause dread.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "4 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "What went wrong",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "People kept editing exported figures by hand “just this once”, which silently broke the link to the script;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Two machines had different font versions, so the same script produced slightly different layouts;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The build file grew into the only documentation of the analysis, and was read by nobody.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We now forbid hand edits in the figures folder, pin font versions in the style file and write a short README per paper.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "5 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Recommendations",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "For a group of our size we recommend starting with one paper, not the whole archive, and keeping the style file under version control from the first day. Compare the time saved with your own numbers using the break-even formula above before you invest the first day.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "References",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
