    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This review surveys machine-learning methods for the discovery of inorganic crystalline materials, in work published between 2016 and 2026. We organise the literature into three themes (property prediction, generative design and active learning), compare representative methods and their reported accuracy, and identify four open challenges: scarce experimental data, uncertainty quantification, multi-objective design and reproducibility.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
