      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Between 278 and 293 K the output of the loam cylinders drifted by less than 0.004 m³ m⁻³, smaller than the calibration error and therefore negligible for irrigation decisions.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "sec:discussion",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A sand-specific model lowers the RMSE of the pooled model (0.019 m³ m⁻³) to 0.012 m³ m⁻³, a 37% reduction, whereas the clay-specific model (0.021 m³ m⁻³) is no better than the pooled one. This agrees with the explanation that the dielectric response of bound water in clay is the dominant error source ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "Berg2019"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Salinity was not varied here and is the main limitation: in saline soils the probes read high",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Electrical conductivity above about 2 dS m⁻¹ was not tested.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A 3 USD capacitive probe reaches an RMSE of 0.012 to 0.021 m³ m⁻³ after a quadratic, soil-specific calibration. A pooled calibration is sufficient for coarse scheduling (0.019 m³ m⁻³), but texture-specific models should be used when the error budget is tighter. Future work will add salinity as a second predictor.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
