    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plasterboard partitions with a cavity are the standard lightweight wall. We measured the weighted sound reduction index Rw of three configurations in a laboratory test facility and compared the results with the mass law and with the mass–air–mass resonance frequency. Doubling the board mass raised Rw by 5 dB, while a 100 mm cavity with mineral wool added a further 9 dB, reaching 45 dB. The resonance frequency of 85 Hz predicted from the cavity depth lies below the building-acoustics range, so the wall performs close to the double-leaf ideal.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
