{
  "children": [
    {
      "text": "\\author{\\IEEEauthorblockN{Sofia Marin}\n\\IEEEauthorblockA{\\textit{Dept. of Electrical Engineering}\\\\\n\\textit{Aldermere Polytechnic}\\\\\nAldermere, Country\\\\\nsofia.marin@example.edu}\n\\and\n\\IEEEauthorblockN{Kwame Boateng}\n\\IEEEauthorblockA{\\textit{Wireless Systems Group}\\\\\n\\textit{Example Networks Lab}\\\\\nRiverton, Country\\\\\nk.boateng@example.org}}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Energy-Aware Duty-Cycle Scheduling for Class A LoRaWAN Sensor Nodes",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Battery life limits long-range wireless sensor networks, and most of the energy of a LoRaWAN node goes into transmitting. We propose a scheduler that picks the spreading factor and the reporting interval of each node from its measured collision probability. In a simulation of 500 nodes around one gateway the scheduler raised the packet delivery ratio from 78.4% to 94.2% and cut the energy per uplink by 34%, which extends the expected battery life from 2.1 to 3.2 years.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "LoRaWAN · duty cycle · energy efficiency · wireless sensor networks · scheduling",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Low-power wide-area networks connect sensors that must run for years on a battery. In LoRaWAN, a Class A node sends an uplink whenever it has data and opens two short receive windows afterwards ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "Adel2019"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Because nodes share the channel by pure ALOHA, collisions grow with the number of nodes, and every lost uplink wastes the energy spent on it.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The contributions of this paper are: (i) an energy and collision model for Class A nodes; (ii) a distributed scheduler that needs no extra downlink traffic; and (iii) a simulation study with 500 nodes.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Related Work",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The adaptive data rate (ADR) mechanism of LoRaWAN selects the spreading factor from the link margin ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "Adel2019"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". It ignores the load of the cell. Scheduling approaches that assign time slots need tight synchronisation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "Chen2020"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which Class A nodes do not have. Our scheduler keeps the ALOHA access and only tunes the offered load.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "System Model",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Collision probability",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "With ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " nodes sending at rate ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with time on air ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the normalised offered load is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "G = N\\lambda T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the probability that an uplink survives is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "P_s = e^{-2G}",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:aloha",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Energy per uplink",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A node spends ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "P_{tx}T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " on transmission, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E_{rx}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the receive windows and sleeps for the rest of the period ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T_c",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "E_u = P_{tx}\\,T + E_{rx} + P_{sleep}\\,(T_c - T)",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:energy",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The energy per delivered message is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E_u / P_s",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", so lowering ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
