      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "sec:disc",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Our results support a modest increase over the tightest common setting. The gain is small in absolute terms, about 12 wpm, but it comes at the cost of roughly 15% more vertical space and is free of any other interface change. We caution against extrapolating beyond short articles, 16 px type and 32-character lines; larger studies should vary these jointly. Our participants were also young and mostly university affiliated, and the three articles, although matched on length and difficulty, are a small sample of text.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Design implications are straightforward:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "default to a line height near 1.4 for body text on phones;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "do not trade readability for density by going below 1.2;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "offer the setting to readers with low vision, who were not part of our sample.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "sec:concl",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "In a controlled study, a line height of 1.4 gave faster and more comfortable phone reading than 1.2, and 1.6 added nothing. We hope these numbers help practitioners set defensible defaults.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Materials and anonymised data are available on request from the first author.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
