        {
          "text": "KT 2134 was observed continuously for 27 d at a 2-min cadence. We used simple aperture photometry, removed points flagged for scattered light, and divided by a low-order polynomial fit per orbit. The resulting light curve has 17,420 points and a point-to-point scatter of 0.12 per cent. High-resolution spectra from a ground-based echelle spectrograph gave the stellar parameters in Table ",
