          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "The decay law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Suppose a sample contains ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N(t)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " nuclei at time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Each nucleus has the same probability per unit time ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " of decaying, independent of its age and of its surroundings. In a short interval ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\mathrm{d}t",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the number of decays is therefore proportional to the number of nuclei present,",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{\\mathrm{d}N}{\\mathrm{d}t}=-\\lambda N,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "and integrating from the initial population ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N_{0}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives the exponential law",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "N(t)=N_{0} e^{-\\lambda t}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The constant ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the decay constant, measured in ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "{\\mathrm{s}}^{-1}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the mean lifetime is its inverse, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tau =1/\\lambda",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "1.2 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Half-life and activity",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Definition (Half-life). ",
          "marks": [
            "bold",
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "The half-life ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "t_{1/2}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the time after which half of an initial population has decayed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Setting ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N=N_{0}/2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "(2)",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "t_{1/2}=\\frac{\\ln{2}}{\\lambda}\\approx 0.693 \\tau .",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "What a detector counts is not ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " but the activity ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A=\\lambda N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the number of decays per second. Its SI unit is the becquerel (1 Bq = 1 decay per second)",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Because ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A\\propto N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the activity obeys the same exponential law as the population, with the same half-life.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " lists five isotopes whose half-lives span seven orders of magnitude.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Isotope",
          "Half-life",
          "$\\lambda$ (s$^{-1}$)",
          "Typical use"
        ],
        [
          "Tc-99m",
          "6.01 h",
          "$3.20\\times10^{-5}$",
          "medical imaging"
