    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This report presents the results of the 2025 monitoring programme on the River Calder and its four main tributaries. Twenty-four sites were sampled monthly for nutrients, dissolved oxygen, and faecal indicator organisms. Overall water quality improved at nineteen sites compared with 2024. Phosphorus remains the principal concern: eleven sites exceeded the 0.05 mg/L good-status threshold, mostly downstream of sewage treatment works.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The main findings are:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "median total phosphorus fell from 0.071 to 0.058 mg/L across the catchment;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "dissolved oxygen met the standard at all sites in every month except July at Holme Bridge;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bathing-water classification at Calder Weir improved from sufficient to good.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
