{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Persistent Currents of Cold Atoms in a Ring Lattice",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Elena Marchetti",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Rings of ultracold atoms are a clean testbed for superfluid flow. This thesis studies a Bose-Einstein condensate of 87Rb loaded into a ring-shaped optical lattice with 24 sites, and asks how long a quantized circulation survives when the lattice depth is raised. We derive a Bose-Hubbard description of the ring, measure the decay of the winding number with time, and find lifetimes that grow from 0.4 s to 5.2 s as the depth goes from 2 to 10 recoil energies. The decay is explained by thermally activated phase slips across the weakest link of the ring.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\tableofcontents",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:intro",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Why rings?",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A superfluid in a ring can carry a flow that never stops. Whereas a stirred cup of water comes to rest within seconds, the wave function of a condensate must return to itself after one trip around the ring, so the circulation is quantized in units of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\hbar/m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " per unit radius. Such persistent currents have been observed in helium and, more recently, in dilute atomic gases ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "ramanathan2011",
            "moulder2012"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The ring lattice added in this work breaks the ring into ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N=24",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " sites. It turns the continuous superfluid into a chain of weakly coupled condensates, in which a phase slip becomes a discrete, countable event.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Contributions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The main results of this thesis are the following:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a Bose-Hubbard model of the ring whose parameters are fixed by a band-structure calculation rather than fitted;",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a measurement of the winding-number lifetime as a function of lattice depth (Table 3.1);",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a thermal phase-slip model that reproduces the lifetimes within their uncertainty.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Outline",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Chapter ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "ch:theory",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " derives the lattice Hamiltonian and the energy barrier for a phase slip. Chapter ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "ch:exp",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " describes the apparatus and the lifetime measurements and compares them with theory.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Theory of the ring lattice",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:theory",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Bose-Hubbard model",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "For a lattice deep enough that only the lowest band is populated, the atoms are described by the Bose-Hubbard Hamiltonian",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\hat H = -J\\sum_{j=1}^{N}\\left(\\hat a_{j+1}^{\\dagger}\\hat a_j + \\mathrm{h.c.}\\right) + \\frac{U}{2}\\sum_{j=1}^{N}\\hat n_j(\\hat n_j-1),",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:bh",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "J",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the tunnelling amplitude between neighbouring sites, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "U",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the on-site interaction, and sites are identified modulo ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". For ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "U/J",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " small, the mean-field ansatz ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\psi_j=\\sqrt{n}\\,e^{i\\varphi_j}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " turns Eq. (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:bh",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": ") into a classical chain of phases, and a current-carrying state has ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\varphi_{j+1}-\\varphi_j = 2\\pi w/N",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with integer winding number ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "w",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Energy barrier for a phase slip",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The energy per site of the state with winding ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "w",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E(w) = -2Jn\\cos(2\\pi w/N)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", so the current is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "I_w = (2\\pi Jn/\\hbar N)\\sin(2\\pi w/N)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The state is metastable as long as the phase step stays below ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\pi/2",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", i.e. for ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "w<N/4",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". We write the barrier as",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\Delta E(w) = 2Jn\\left[\\cos\\frac{2\\pi (w-1)}{N} - \\cos\\frac{2\\pi w}{N}\\right] \\approx \\frac{4\\pi J n}{N}\\,\\sin\\frac{2\\pi w}{N}\\,\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{N}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:barrier",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The barrier shrinks with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "J",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which falls exponentially with lattice depth ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "V_0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The simple estimate below, valid for ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "V_0 \\gtrsim 2E_r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", shows the trend that the experiment tests:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{J}{E_r} \\simeq \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}\\left(\\frac{V_0}{E_r}\\right)^{3/4}e^{-2\\sqrt{V_0/E_r}}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:jfit",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Here ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E_r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the photon recoil energy of the lattice light. Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:jfit",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the Mathieu-equation asymptote",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "See any treatment of the lowest band of the Mathieu equation for the full expression.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the numerical values used below come from the exact band structure.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Experiment and results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
