      "caption": "Winding-number lifetime of the w = 1 state against lattice depth.",
      "label": "tab:life",
      "alignment": "rrrr",
      "style": "booktabs",
      "merges": [],
      "header": true,
      "repeat_header": false,
      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The lifetime grows roughly linearly with the barrier, as expected for a thermally activated process with an attempt rate of order 1 Hz at the temperature of 22 nK. A fit of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tau = \\tau_0\\exp(\\Delta E/k_B T)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " gives ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\tau_0 = 0.09\\pm0.03\\ \\mathrm{s}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A deeper ring lattice stabilizes persistent flow by suppressing tunnelling across the weakest link, with lifetimes that follow the activated form of Eq. ",
