      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Giulia Ferraresi",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This thesis reads six nineteenth-century travel narratives of the Mediterranean to ask how port cities were made legible to a northern readership. It argues that the harbour, rather than the monument, is the organizing image of these texts, and that the travellers' descriptions of markets, quarantine and languages record a commercial cosmopolitanism that later national histories erased.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\tableofcontents",
      "type": "RawLatex"
