      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:market",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Two scenes recur in almost every narrative: the market, where languages are heard together, and the lazaretto, where travellers wait out the quarantine. They are opposite experiences of the same city, one open and one enclosed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
