        {
          "text": "Regenerative Braking Control for a Light Electric Vehicle",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Marco Delvaux",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This thesis designs and tests a regenerative braking controller for a 250 kg electric quadricycle with a 4 kW in-wheel motor. A slip-based blending law divides the braking demand between the motor and the friction brakes. In simulation over a 12 km urban cycle the controller recovers 14.8 per cent of the traction energy and raises the range from 62 to 71 km, with no loss of stopping distance below 8 m from 30 km/h.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\tableofcontents",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:intro",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Light electric vehicles spend most of their energy accelerating a small mass repeatedly, so the share that can be recovered when braking is large ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "rossi2017",
            "haddad2019"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The difficulty is that the motor can brake only within the limits of its torque and of the battery's charge acceptance, while the driver expects the same pedal feel as with friction brakes.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The objective is a controller that maximizes the recovered energy subject to three constraints: the battery current limit, the wheel-slip limit and the stopping distance.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Specifications",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Recover at least 12 per cent of the traction energy on the urban cycle.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Stop from 30 km/h in no more than 8 m.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Keep the battery charge current below 40 A.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Vehicle model and controller",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "ch:model",
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Longitudinal dynamics",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "With vehicle mass ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "m",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", wheel radius ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and braking force ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "F_b",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the speed ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "v",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " obeys",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "m\\,\\dot v = -F_b - \\tfrac{1}{2}\\rho C_d A\\,v^{2} - C_{rr}\\,m g,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:long",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\rho",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the air density, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "C_d A",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the drag area and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "C_{rr}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rolling resistance coefficient. The braking force splits into a regenerative part and a friction part,",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "F_b = F_{\\mathrm{reg}} + F_{\\mathrm{fric}},\\qquad F_{\\mathrm{reg}} = \\min\\!\\left(\\beta F_{\\mathrm{dem}},\\ \\frac{T_{\\max}}{r}\\right),",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:blend",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "with demand ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "F_{\\mathrm{dem}}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", motor torque limit ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T_{\\max}=95\\ \\mathrm{N\\,m}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and blending gain ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta\\in[0,1]",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:blend",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " sends as much braking as possible to the motor, and the friction brakes supply the remainder.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Parameters",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Parameter",
          "Value",
          "Unit"
        ],
        [
          "Vehicle mass",
          "250",
          "kg"
        ],
        [
