    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The speed of sound in air was measured with a closed resonance tube and three tuning forks (256, 440 and 512 Hz). From the spacing of the first two resonances at each frequency we obtain v = 341.6 ± 0.8 m/s at 21.3 °C, 0.8% below the accepted value of 344.2 m/s. The end correction measured independently, 1.2 cm, is close to the theoretical 0.6 r = 1.0 cm.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
