    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "For the Ti 2p doublet the 2p₁/₂ component was tied to 2p₃/₂ with a spin–orbit splitting of 5.72 eV and an area ratio fixed at the degeneracy ratio",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{A(2p_{1/2})}{A(2p_{3/2})} = \\frac{2j_{1/2}+1}{2j_{3/2}+1} = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:ratio",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The 2p₁/₂ width was left free: Coster–Kronig broadening makes it roughly twice that of 2p₃/₂. Atomic concentrations follow from the fitted areas ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
