      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Oxygen vacancies and Ti³⁺ states in reduced anatase TiO₂ thin films probed by X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A. Surface, B. Vacuum and C. Synchrotron",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Department of Materials, Example University",
          "marks": [
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "center",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatase TiO₂ films grown by atomic layer deposition were annealed in ultra-high vacuum between 300 and 700 °C and analysed in situ by monochromated Al Kα XPS. Peak fitting of the Ti 2p region with spin–orbit-constrained doublets on a Shirley background resolves a Ti³⁺ component 1.7 eV below Ti⁴⁺, whose fraction of the Ti 2p signal rises from 2.1 % to 14.0 % with annealing temperature. The O 1s spectra show a concurrent growth of a hydroxyl / vacancy-adjacent component at 531.3 eV. An Arrhenius analysis of the Ti³⁺ fraction gives an apparent activation energy of 0.23 ± 0.01 eV for vacancy formation.",
          "marks": [
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Keywords: ",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "XPS · TiO₂ · oxygen vacancies · peak fitting · Shirley background",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "1 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Titanium dioxide is the archetypal photocatalyst, and its activity is governed to a large extent by point defects at the surface ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "[1]",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Removal of lattice oxygen leaves two excess electrons that localise on neighbouring Ti sites, producing Ti³⁺ centres with a characteristic chemical shift in the Ti 2p spectrum ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "[2]",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Quantifying that component reliably requires a physically constrained fit; in this work we describe a protocol and apply it to a temperature series.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Experimental",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.1 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sample preparation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Films of nominal thickness 30 nm were grown on Si(100) by thermal ALD from TiCl₄ and H₂O at 250 °C (600 cycles at 0.5 Å per cycle) and crystallised to anatase by a 1 h anneal in air at 450 °C, confirmed by Raman spectroscopy (Eg mode at 144 cm⁻¹). Each film was then annealed for 30 min in the analysis chamber at 300, 400, 500, 600 or 700 °C and cooled to room temperature before measurement.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.2 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "XPS acquisition",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Monochromated Al Kα (hν = 1486.6 eV), 400 µm spot",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pass energy 20 eV for core levels, 150 eV for surveys",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Charge neutraliser on; energy scale referenced to adventitious C 1s at 284.8 eV",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Base pressure < 5 × 10⁻¹⁰ mbar during acquisition",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.3 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Peak fitting",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each component was modelled with a pseudo-Voigt line shape, a Gaussian–Lorentzian sum with mixing parameter ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\eta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and full width at half maximum ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "I(E)=A\\left[\\eta \\frac{1}{1+4{\\left(\\frac{E-E_{0}}{\\beta}\\right)}^{2}}+(1-\\eta ) \\exp{}\\left(-4\\ln{2}{\\left(\\frac{E-E_{0}}{\\beta}\\right)}^{2}\\right)\\right]",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The inelastic background was removed with the iterative Shirley algorithm ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "[3]",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": ", in which the background at binding energy ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is proportional to the integrated peak area on the low-binding-energy side of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "E",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "B(E)=B_{\\text{low}}+(B_{\\text{high}}-B_{\\text{low}}) \\frac{\\int_{E_{\\text{low}}}^{E}{[I(E')-B(E')] dE'}}{\\int_{E_{\\text{low}}}^{E_{\\text{high}}}{[I(E')-B(E')] dE'}}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "For the Ti 2p doublet the 2p₁/₂ component was tied to 2p₃/₂ with a spin–orbit splitting of 5.72 eV and an area ratio fixed at the degeneracy ratio",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{A(2p_{1/2})}{A(2p_{3/2})}=\\frac{2j_{1/2}+1}{2j_{3/2}+1}=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The 2p₁/₂ width was left free: Coster–Kronig broadening makes it roughly twice that of 2p₃/₂. Atomic concentrations follow from the fitted areas ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "A_{i}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the relative sensitivity factors ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "S_{i}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " (Scofield cross-sections corrected for transmission and inelastic mean free path):",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "x_{i}=\\frac{A_{i}/S_{i}}{\\sum_{j}{A_{j}/S_{j}}}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "3 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " lists the fitted Ti 2p₃/₂ parameters. The Ti⁴⁺ position is stable to within 0.07 eV across the series, confirming that charge referencing is not responsible for the apparent new component. The Ti³⁺ peak sits 1.7 eV below Ti⁴⁺ throughout. If every Ti³⁺ ion is charge-compensated by half an oxygen vacancy, a Ti³⁺ fraction ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "f",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " corresponds to the stoichiometry TiO",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "{}_{2-f/2}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", given as δ = f/2 in the last column.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Anneal (°C)",
          "Ti⁴⁺ (eV)",
          "Ti³⁺ (eV)",
          "FWHM Ti⁴⁺",
          "f (pct)",
          "δ"
        ],
        [
          "as-grown",
          "458.72",
          "—",
          "0.98",
          "< 1",
          "< 0.005"
        ],
        [
          "300",
          "458.70",
          "457.00",
          "0.99",
          "2.1",
          "0.011"
        ],
        [
          "400",
