      "shading": {},
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Table 2: ",
          "marks": [
            "bold",
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "O 1s component analysis (areas in per cent of the O 1s total).",
          "marks": [
            "italic"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "center",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "4 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Assuming the Ti³⁺ fraction is proportional to the equilibrium vacancy concentration, a plot of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\ln{f}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " against ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "1/T",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is linear (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "R^{2}=0.992",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ") with slope",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\frac{d\\ln{f}}{d(1/T)}=-\\frac{E_{a}}{k_{B}} \\Rightarrow E_{a}=0.23\\pm 0.01 \\text{eV}.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This value is far below the bulk vacancy formation energy predicted by hybrid DFT (≈ 4 eV), so the fraction measured here cannot be an equilibrium bulk property. It is more naturally read as the barrier for oxygen release from the surface in vacuum, with the reducing UHV environment and the entropy of the released O₂ lowering the effective cost.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The information depth of the measurement, taken as three inelastic mean free paths of the Ti 2p photoelectrons (kinetic energy ≈ 1030 eV), is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "d=3\\lambda \\cos{\\theta}\\approx 3\\times 2.1 \\text{nm}\\times \\cos{0^{\\circ}}\\approx 6 \\text{nm},",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "so the Ti³⁺ signal originates from roughly the outermost 16 anatase unit-cell layers (c = 9.5 Å, four TiO₂ layers per cell) of a 30 nm film. Angle-resolved measurements would discriminate surface from sub-surface vacancies.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "5 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Conclusions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "A constrained Ti 2p fit reliably separates Ti³⁺ at −1.7 eV from Ti⁴⁺.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The Ti³⁺ fraction rises monotonically to 14.0 % at 700 °C, i.e. TiO₁.₉₃.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Vacancy formation has an apparent activation energy of 0.23 eV.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
