{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Effect of a 12-week supervised exercise programme on HbA1c in adults with type 2 diabetes: a randomised controlled trial",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "H. Medic, I. Statistician and J. Nurse, on behalf of the MOVE-T2D investigators",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Department of Primary Care, Example University",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Affiliation"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Background: Structured exercise improves glycaemic control, but effect sizes in routine care are uncertain. Methods: 240 adults with type 2 diabetes (HbA1c 7.0–10.0 %) were randomised 1:1 to supervised exercise or usual care. The primary outcome was change in HbA1c at 12 weeks, analysed by intention to treat. Results: HbA1c fell by 0.62 % with exercise versus 0.11 % with usual care (adjusted difference −0.51 %; 95 % CI −0.70 to −0.32; p < 0.001). Conclusions: Supervised exercise produces a clinically meaningful reduction in HbA1c. Trial registration: ISRCTN00000000.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "type 2 diabetes · exercise · RCT · HbA1c",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Type 2 diabetes affects more than 500 million adults worldwide ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "atlas2021"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Guidelines recommend 150 minutes of moderate activity per week, but adherence outside trials is poor. We tested whether a supervised programme delivered in routine primary care lowers HbA1c.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Design and participants",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Parallel-group, assessor-blinded randomised trial at four centres, reported according to the CONSORT 2010 statement ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "schaefer2010"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Randomisation was 1:1, computer-generated in blocks of 4 and 6, stratified by centre, with allocation concealed in sealed web-based envelopes.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Inclusion: age 40–75 y, type 2 diabetes for ≥ 1 y, HbA1c 7.0–10.0 %, stable medication for 3 months",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Exclusion: insulin therapy, unstable angina, eGFR < 30 mL/min/1.73 m²",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Interventions",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The exercise arm attended three supervised 60-minute sessions per week (aerobic and resistance training at moderate to vigorous intensity); usual care participants received standard advice and continued their usual routine.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sample size",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "To detect a difference ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta = 0.4\\,\\%",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with SD ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\sigma = 0.9\\,\\%",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", two-sided ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\alpha = 0.05",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and power 90 %:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "n = \\frac{2\\,(z_{1-\\alpha/2}+z_{1-\\beta})^2\\,\\sigma^2}{\\Delta^2} = \\frac{2(1.96+1.28)^2(0.9)^2}{0.4^2} \\approx 107",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:n",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "per arm; inflating for 10 % attrition gives ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "107/0.9 \\approx 119",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", so 120 per arm were enrolled.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Statistical analysis",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The primary analysis used ANCOVA on the intention-to-treat population, adjusting for baseline and centre:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "Y_{i,12} = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1\\,\\text{Tx}_i + \\beta_2\\,Y_{i,0} + \\sum_c \\gamma_c\\,\\text{Centre}_{ic} + \\epsilon_i,",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:ancova",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta_1",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the adjusted treatment effect. Missing data were handled by multiple imputation (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "m = 50",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ") under missing-at-random, and the results were combined with Rubin's rules. The binary secondary outcome (HbA1c < 7 %, non-completers counted as failures) is summarised by the risk difference and the number needed to treat.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Of 351 adults assessed, 111 were excluded (64 did not meet the criteria, 38 declined and 9 had other reasons) and 240 were randomised, 120 per arm (Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:flow",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": "). Follow-up was 90 % in the exercise arm and 93 % in the usual-care arm; all randomised participants were analysed.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
