        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Green hydrogen from direct solar water splitting could decarbonise heavy industry, but particulate photocatalysts remain below 1 % solar-to-hydrogen (STH) efficiency. SOLAR-CAT combines in-situ spectroscopy, machine-learned defect models and high-throughput synthesis to reach 3 % STH in a 1 m² panel within 36 months, at a total cost of £1.51 M.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
