        },
        {
          "text": "20 May 2026",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "left",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Subject:  ",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Migration from PostgreSQL 14 to 16",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "left",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\noindent\\rule{\\textwidth}{0.4pt}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We propose migrating the production database from PostgreSQL 14 to PostgreSQL 16 during the maintenance window of 7–8 June 2026. The upgrade brings the logical-replication improvements that unblock the event-sourcing work planned for Q3 and removes our dependency on a version that is about to lose community support.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Background",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "PostgreSQL 14 reaches community end-of-life in November 2026",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Per the project's published versioning policy, each major release is supported for five years.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "Footnote"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Several extensions we depend on (pg_partman, pgvector) have already dropped CI testing against it, so staying put raises the risk of compatibility regressions with every extension update.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
